{# The first part of the one bar above the grid of a page of photos to pick (0305): where
   you are (`#status`), or, once files are picked, what to do with them; then the line of
   what is set aside (`#chosen`) and *Apply now*. `pickAll` (a search shows its first files
   only) picks every file found. The page adds its own fields after it, in the bar; a
   page where a pick means something else names its two actions (`pick_add`,
   `pick_remove`). Order (0542): the page's most used action first (`pick_first`, a template
   holding a `primary` button), *Set aside* last, red (`danger`), apart. ▶ *Slideshow* ▾ (0660, `tv_here`: a page served by the home server)
   shows the files picked, or every file the page shows, on this PC or on the TV. #}
<span id="lead"><span id="status" role="status"></span></span>
<span id="acting" hidden>
  <button id="unpick" class="plain" type="button" title="{{ _('Pick none') }}" aria-label="{{ _('Pick none') }}">✕</button>
  <strong id="picked"></strong>
  <button id="pickAll" class="plain" type="button" hidden></button>
  {% if pick_first is string and pick_first.endswith(".html.j2") %}{% include pick_first %}{% endif %}
  <button id="takeBack" class="plain" type="button" hidden title="{{ _('Take out of the set aside (Backspace in the large view)') }}">{{ pick_remove | default("↩ " + _("Take out of the set aside")) }}</button>
  <button id="invert" class="plain" type="button" title="{{ _('Pick the others: the ones picked are left (I)') }}">🔀 {{ _("Invert the picking") }}</button>
  <button id="setAside" class="danger" type="button" title="{{ pick_add_title | default(_('Set aside the picked files (Delete)')) }}">{{ pick_add | default("🗑 " + _("Put aside")) }}</button>
</span>
{% if tv_here | default(false) %}{% include "slideshow_menu.html.j2" %}{% endif %}
<span id="chosen" role="status"></span>
{% include "apply_now.html.j2" %}
